# Force LF line endings for snapshot fixtures so Windows CI doesn't
# fail comparisons after git's autocrlf converts checkouts to CRLF.
*.stderr text eol=lf

# The fix-fixture input/expected trees are byte-compared after checkout
# (tests/fix_fixtures.rs reads each file to a String and asserts equality).
# A setup.toml `[[append]]` hook injects directive lines with LF, so a Windows
# CRLF checkout would desync the two sides. Force LF across the fixture trees
# so the comparison is platform-independent.
crates/workspace-lint/tests/fixtures/** text eol=lf

# Committed rust-analyzer SCIP indexes for the deep `--fix` fixtures are binary
# protobuf — never apply EOL conversion, or a Windows checkout would corrupt
# them and `ScipIndex::load` would fail to decode.
*.scip binary
